ummary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nWith cmake function find_library, it returns an invalid path for libsimdjson.a.\r\n\r\n**Environment**\r\n- OS: Mac OS\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\r\n1. ./vcpkg install simdjson\r\n2. in my project CMakeLists.txt, add \r\n```cmake\r\nfind_path(SIMDJSON_INCLUDE_DIR simdjson)\r\nmessage(\"SIMDJSON_INCLUDE_DIR: ${SIMDJSON_INCLUDE_DIR}\")\r\nfind_library(SIMDJSON_LIBRARY NAMES simdjson)\r\nmessage(\"SIMDJSON_LIBRARY: ${SIMDJSON_LIBRARY}\")\r\n\r\ntarget_include_directories(main PUBLIC ${SIMDJSON_INCLUDE_DIR})\r\ntarget_link_libraries(main ${SIMDJSON_LIBRARY})\r\n```\r\ngot output\r\n```\r\nSIMDJSON_INCLUDE_DIR: .../vcpkg/installed/x64-osx/include\r\nSIMDJSON_LIBRARY: .../vcpkg/installed/x64-osx/debug/lib/libsimdjson.a\r\n```\r\n3. compile project and got linker failures\r\n4. change the last line of CMakeLists.txt to \r\n```cmake\r\ntarget_link_libraries(main .../vcpkg/installed/x64-osx/lib/libsimdjson.a)\r\n```\r\n5. compile project and it succeeded\r\n\r\n**Questions**\r\nWith find_library(SIMDJSON_LIBRARY NAMES simdjson), it returned SIMDJSON_LIBRARY with value .../vcpkg/installed/x64-osx/debug/lib/libsimdjson.a which failed. And the path \".../vcpkg/installed/x64-osx/lib/libsimdjson.a\" succeeded.\r\n1. What's the difference between the two libs and why the first one fails?\r\n2. Why the function find_library doesn't find .../vcpkg/installed/x64-osx/lib/libsimdjson.a?\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"dan-shaw","id":51385773,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzg1Nzcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51385773?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-shaw","html_url":"https://github.com/dan-shaw","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-shaw/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-shaw/following{/ot